@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
       "_": "Phase 0 step 2 ORDERS a read of this file. ⚠ MEASURED 3,946,063 B / 13,912 lines at Session 255 -- 33x this ceiling, and larger than BOTH ledgers were before the Session 254 trim. Sessions 254 and 255 each read ~160 lines of it and inferred the rest, which is failure mode #28 committed twice by the session that then wrote the finding down. The ceiling is canonical's, kept deliberately rather than raised to make this green -- raising it would record the problem as the standard. Reducing this file is a NAMED next deliverable, not housekeeping."
     },
     {
-      "path": "HANDOFFS.md",
+      "path": "methodology/HANDOFFS.md",
       "class": "read-mandated",
       "max_bytes": 65536,
       "_": "The durable receipt ledger; Phase 0 reconciles it and Phase 3D writes to it. 65,536 B is this project's ceiling, no longer the trimmer's: trim v1.5.0 (synced at Session 264) archives it only above 196,608 B, so this entry stays `over` until a trim is run by hand. KEPT deliberately: the operator decided at methodology Session 191 (the upstream plan's D7) that the remedy is a trim in this project, not dropping the warning as CHANGELOG.md's was -- and that trim needs `--budget-bytes` or `--cut N --force`, since the trimmer's own trigger will not fire. 52,850 B after the Session 254 trim (was 1,801,150 -- 27x over, refusing to trim at all because of a stale bootstrap seed footer); 62,521 B when this config was written at Session 255. Measure, don't trust this sentence: `python3 methodology_trim.py --check --file HANDOFFS.md`."
